sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (Nick approved 2026-11-07): a provision claims a slot. Slots are fixed, reused task VMs named <node>-tvm-<slot>, each a permanent Orbit Node whose identity was written once at enroll. The image holds everything. The image is baked by the refresh (docs/cli/tasks/vm-image-refresh.mmd).
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: tasks:provision
  %% kind: tasks.provision
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=slot tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant VM as Slot<br/>shark-tvm-3
  Note over GW: Claim a free slot<br/>one run per group
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `tasks:provision` for a todo group, from proof CI or feature work; the same slots serve both
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - a free slot on the host, enrolled from the promoted image
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the group holds `shark-tvm-3`; its Node, WireGuard peer, agent secret, Pi token and host key already exist, so nothing is minted or published
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-tasks-provision
  SW->>H: Start the slot<br/>incus start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `incus start shark-tvm-3`; about 7 s to the guest agent
  %%> - the agent, Pi, WireGuard, the tools, the warm checkout of main and the containers are all on its disk
  SW->>VM: Fetch the task branch<br/>onto the warm checkout
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `git fetch` of the group's branch with an App read token minted for this step, then checkout; the token never stays on the VM
  %%> - `composer install` or `npm ci` only when a lock file differs from main's
  SW->>VM: Start the containers<br/>from base
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - restore `base` and start Gateway+Swamp, app-dev and app-prod; 3.5 to 7 s each
  %%> - migrations run only when the branch adds new ones
  SW->>VM: Check ready<br/>one exec
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one exec checks the agent, Pi, the tunnel and the three containers; Swamp's `assert` decides
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>ready
    Note over GW: Record the slot ready<br/>target under 30 s
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the slot is released (stopped and rolled back to `clean`); the group records the failed step
  end
